From: Andrei Nigmatulin <andrei.nigmatulin@gmail.com>
Subject: hostapd: WPS: hand out a wpa_psk_file entry's passphrase

Entries of wpa_psk_file marked wps=1 are the WPS credential. hostapd keeps
only the derived PSK of each entry and hands that out in 64-hex format,
which some Enrollees (e.g. thermostats with Hi-Flying Wi-Fi modules) cannot
use. Keep the passphrase of entries given as one and hand it out instead.

With this, a WPS session for one device needs no configuration change: the
entry is marked wps=1 in the PSK file (re-read in place), and the
push-button window opened with wps_start.

